  { slug: 'blog/dog-poop-cleanup-chattanooga-summer-heat', title: 'Dog Poop Cleanup in Chattanooga During Hot, Humid Weather | Scoopy Doo', desc: 'Summer heat and humidity make dog waste more dangerous. Learn why Chattanooga yards need regular cleanup during the hot months and how Scoopy Doo can help.', canonical: 'https://www.scoopychatt.com/blog/dog-poop-cleanup-chattanooga-summer-heat', body: '<h1>Dog Poop Cleanup in Chattanooga During Hot, Humid Weather</h1><p>Dog waste becomes significantly more dangerous during Chattanooga summers. Bacteria in dog feces multiply twice as fast when temperatures exceed 90 degrees Fahrenheit, and Chattanooga regularly sees 90 to 95 degree days from June through September. The result is faster odor, faster lawn damage, and higher health risk for kids and pets who play in the yard.</p><h2>Why Summer Heat Makes Dog Waste More Urgent</h2><p>At high temperatures, bacteria like E. coli and Salmonella in dog waste reach dangerous concentrations faster. Flies spread these bacteria from waste to surfaces throughout your yard. Parasites including roundworm and hookworm eggs survive longer in warm, moist soil. In Chattanooga\'s humid summers, the combination of heat and moisture creates ideal conditions for all of these.</p><h2>Lawn Damage Is Worse in Summer</h2><p>Dog waste kills grass at any temperature, but the damage accelerates in summer heat. The high nitrogen concentration in dog feces burns already heat-stressed turf. Brown patches that might recover in cooler months often become permanent dead spots when waste sits on summer lawns. Weekly removal is the only reliable way to prevent accumulating damage.</p><h2>Smell Travels Further in Hot Weather</h2><p>Heat intensifies odors. A yard that seems manageable in March can become unpleasant for neighbors and outdoor dining by July. Consistent weekly removal keeps odor from building between visits.</p><h2>How Scoopy Doo Handles Chattanooga Summers</h2><p>Scoopy Doo technicians run routes 7 days a week through Chattanooga summers. Weekly service visits include a full grid-pattern yard sweep, double-bag removal of all waste into your outdoor bin or off the property for $5 per visit, an on-the-way text, and a gate photo after every visit. Most Chattanooga customers find weekly service to be the right frequency during summer months with one or two dogs.</p><h2>Get a Free Quote</h2><p>Weekly service starts at $20 per visit for one dog. No contracts required. Request a free quote at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest and Scoopy Doo responds the same day.</p>' },
  { slug: 'blog/how-often-clean-yard', title: 'How Often Should You Clean Your Yard of Dog Waste? | Scoopy Doo', desc: 'Weekly is the gold standard. Learn the right cleanup frequency based on your dog count, yard size, and Chattanooga season.', canonical: 'https://www.scoopychatt.com/blog/how-often-clean-yard', body: '<h1>How Often Should You Clean Your Yard of Dog Waste?</h1><p>Weekly is the gold standard for most Chattanooga households with one or two dogs. Dog waste should never sit in a yard for more than a week. Beyond one week, bacteria multiply to dangerous levels, fly activity increases, lawn damage worsens, and odor builds. Weekly professional service eliminates all of these problems consistently.</p><h2>By Number of Dogs</h2><p>One dog produces roughly 274 pounds of waste per year. Two dogs double that. For one or two dogs, weekly service keeps waste from accumulating between visits. For three or more dogs, every-other-week visits may not be sufficient and twice-weekly service is worth considering. Scoopy Doo offers weekly, every-other-week, and twice-weekly service depending on your household.</p><h2>By Yard Size</h2><p>Larger yards can look clean longer while still harboring significant waste. A half-acre yard with one dog might seem fine after two weeks but still have accumulated enough waste to damage turf and create health risks. Smaller yards show waste and smell faster. In either case, weekly service is the most reliable approach.</p><h2>By Season in Chattanooga</h2><p>Chattanooga summers require the most frequent service. Heat and humidity accelerate bacterial growth and odor. Winter service is still necessary because dog waste does not decompose safely in cold weather and parasites survive in frozen soil. Year-round weekly service is the most common choice for Scoopy Doo customers.</p><h2>Signs You Need More Frequent Service</h2><ul><li>Visible waste within 2 or 3 days of a cleanup visit</li><li>Brown or yellow patches appearing in your lawn</li><li>Noticeable odor when you open the back door</li><li>Kids or pets tracking waste onto patios or into the house</li></ul><h2>Scoopy Doo Pricing by Frequency</h2><p>Weekly service starts at $20 per visit for one dog in Chattanooga. Every-other-week starts at $33 per visit. One-time cleanups start at $85. No contracts. Free quotes at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest.</p>' },
  { slug: 'blog/chattanooga-pet-waste-removal-homeowners', title: 'Pet Waste Removal for Chattanooga Homeowners | Scoopy Doo', desc: 'Why Chattanooga homeowners hire professional pet waste removal: time savings, lawn health, and protection for kids and pets. Starting at $20/visit.', canonical: 'https://www.scoopychatt.com/blog/chattanooga-pet-waste-removal-homeowners', body: '<h1>Why Chattanooga Homeowners Hire a Professional Pet Waste Removal Service</h1><p>Professional pet waste removal saves Chattanooga homeowners time, protects their lawns, and eliminates a task that most people dislike. Scoopy Doo serves homes across Chattanooga and North Georgia with weekly service starting at $20 per visit for one dog. No contracts required.</p><h2>Time Savings</h2><p>The average dog owner spends 20 to 30 minutes per week cleaning up pet waste. Over a year, that is 17 to 26 hours. Professional service reclaims that time completely. The cost of weekly service is less than most streaming subscriptions and frees up yard time for things that are actually enjoyable.</p><h2>Lawn Health</h2><p>Dog waste kills grass. The high nitrogen concentration in dog feces burns turf, especially during hot Chattanooga summers. Waste that sits for more than a few days creates brown spots that are difficult to recover. Weekly professional removal is the most reliable way to prevent cumulative lawn damage from dog waste.</p><h2>Health Protection for Kids and Pets</h2><p>Dog waste carries E. coli, Salmonella, roundworm, hookworm, and other pathogens that remain active in soil long after the waste itself is gone. Children who play in yards with accumulated waste are at genuine risk. Weekly removal keeps pathogen levels from building to dangerous concentrations.</p><h2>What Scoopy Doo Includes on Every Visit</h2><ul><li>On-the-way text notification before the technician arrives</li><li>Full yard swept in a systematic grid pattern</li><li>All waste double-bagged into your outdoor bin, or hauled off the property for $5 per visit</li><li>Gate photo confirmation after every visit</li></ul><p>Service is available 7 days a week throughout Chattanooga, Hixson, Red Bank, Signal Mountain, Ooltewah, East Brainerd, Soddy-Daisy, Cleveland, East Ridge, Lookout Mountain TN, and Ringgold, Rossville, Fort Oglethorpe, Flintstone GA.</p><h2>Pricing</h2><p>Weekly service starts at $20 per visit for one dog. Every-other-week starts at $33 per visit. One-time yard cleanups start at $85. No contracts, no cancellation fees. Request a free quote at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest and Scoopy Doo responds the same day.</p>' }
